          hinge_question:
            'Why was the social freedom of the "New Woman" celebrated as a triumph of Weimar democracy by urban liberals, while being fiercely condemned as moral degeneracy by rural conservatives?',
          source_context:
            'During the 1920s, the Weimar Republic granted women universal suffrage and constitutional equality, leading to the cultural phenomenon of the "New Woman" (Neue Frau), although economic disparity and traditional social prejudice remained pervasive. **Hinge Question:** Why was the social freedom of the "New Woman" celebrated as a triumph of Weimar democracy by urban liberals, while being fiercely condemned as moral degeneracy by rural conservatives?',
          context:
            'Contemporary essay by Alice Rühle-Gerstel published in Die literarische Welt in September 1927.',
