          act: 5,
          text: '<p><span class="para-ref">[5.1]</span> The final constitutional barrier fell on 2 August 1934 when 86-year-old President Paul von Hindenburg died at his Neudeck estate. Hours before his death, Hitler\'s cabinet merged the offices of Chancellor and President into a single supreme title: Führer und Reichskanzler. Hitler absorbed all executive authority, emergency powers, and supreme military command, later confirming the consolidation through a manipulated national plebiscite polling 89.9% approval.</p>\n\n<p><span class="para-ref">[5.2]</span> That same afternoon, all officers and soldiers in the German armed forces were required to swear a new oath of allegiance. Instead of pledging loyalty to the constitution or nation, every serviceman swore absolute personal obedience to Adolf Hitler: \'I will render unconditional obedience to the Leader of the German Reich and people, Adolf Hitler.\' Bound by this sacred military honour code, the army was locked into Hitler\'s totalitarian dictatorship.</p>',
