              type: 'written',
              text: "The Reich Government has enacted the following law, which is hereby promulgated:\nArticle 1. For the prosecution of offenses of high treason and treason against the state, a People's Court (Volksgerichtshof) shall be established.\nArticle 2. The People's Court shall consist of professional judges appointed by the Reich Chancellor for a term of five years, and honorary members selected from the Schutzstaffel (SS), the SA, and the National Socialist German Workers' Party upon the proposal of the Führer's Deputy.\nArticle 3. The proceedings shall be conducted without a jury. From the decisions of the People's Court there shall be no appeal and no legal remedy of any kind. The accused may only choose defence counsel from a list approved by the President of the Court.",
