          act: 4,
          text: "<p><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> In August 1936, the regime exploited the Berlin Olympic Games as an extraordinary international public relations spectacle to showcase the rebirth of Nazi Germany. Goebbels spared no expense, erecting a colossal 100,000-seat Olympic Stadium in Berlin and pioneering live television broadcasts. To deceive foreign dignitaries and international tourists, anti-Semitic signs ('Jews Not Wanted') were quietly removed from Berlin's streets, anti-Jewish violence was suspended, and jazz music was temporarily tolerated in nightspots.</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> The games aimed to provide scientific proof of Aryan racial superiority, with Germany successfully topping the medal table with 33 gold medals. However, the regime's racial ideology was famously challenged by the triumphs of African American athlete Jesse Owens. Owens won four Olympic gold medals (100m, 200m, 4x100m relay, long jump), setting world records and earning thunderous ovations from ordinary German spectators, visibly puncturing Hitler's myth of racial supremacy despite the lavish state spectacle.</p>",
