          text: 'I\'m beginning to comprehend some of the reasons for Hitler\'s astonishing success... He is restoring pageantry and colour and mystical excitement to a people whose lives have been drab and gray since the defeat of 1918. When he entered the stadium, a sea of arms went up and a roar of "Heil!" shook the earth. It is not just obedience; it is a religious frenzy. These people look upon Hitler not as a politician, but as a redeemer sent by Providence. The vast night assemblies under the giant searchlights—Speer\'s "cathedral of light"—produce an optical and acoustic hypnosis that overwhelms individual critical thought. In that vast throng, even a detached foreigner feels the magnetic pull of the herd.',
