          text: '“§ 1. Anyone who is suffering from a hereditary disease may be rendered sterile by surgical operation if, according to medical science, there is a high probability that their descendants will suffer from severe physical or mental hereditary defects. Hereditary diseases under this law include: congenital feeblemindedness, schizophrenia, hereditary epilepsy, hereditary blindness or deafness, severe hereditary physical deformity, and severe alcoholism.\n§ 2. The operation may also be requested by the official physician or the director of a hospital or psychiatric asylum.\n§ 12. Once the Hereditary Health Court has decided on sterilization, the operation must be carried out, even against the will of the person concerned, using police force if necessary.”',
