          title:
            'Source E: Secret Sopade Intelligence Report on Compulsory Female Labour (December 1938)',
          type: 'written',
          text: "“The contradiction in Nazi propaganda regarding women has now become grotesque. For five years, women were told that their place was exclusively in the home and that working women were destroying family life. Now, because of Hermann Göring’s Four-Year Plan and the severe shortage of male factory workers due to military expansion, the regime is desperately dragging women back into industry. Young unmarried women are compelled to perform a compulsory 'Duty Year' (Pflichtjahr) on farms or in domestic service, and factories are openly recruiting female machinists. In Berlin and Saxony, married women who gave up their jobs in 1933 are being pressured by the Labour Exchanges to take 50-hour factory shifts. Working-class women laugh bitterly at the old slogan 'Kinder, Küche, Kirche'—now it is 'Kinder, Küche, Krupp'.”",
