              text: '“§ 1. The Reich Labour Service is a service of honour to the German people. All young Germans of both sexes are obliged to serve their people in the Reich Labour Service (RAD).\n§ 2. The RAD shall educate German youth in the spirit of National Socialism to acquire a true national community, a true concept of work, and above all, due respect for manual labour.\n§ 3. The RAD is intended to carry out public utility works beneficial to the entire nation.\n§ 8. All young male Germans between their 18th and 25th birthdays are liable to complete six months of compulsory manual labour service before being called up for military service.”',
