          text: "<p><span class=\"para-ref\">[1.1]</span> Minorities persecution was the ideological core of Hitler's National Socialist worldview. Rooted in pseudo-scientific Social Darwinism, Nazi doctrine viewed history as an existential struggle between races. At the apex stood the 'Aryan' master race (Herrenvolk)—depicted as Germanic culture-creators—while Slavic peoples were deemed inferior, and Jews and Roma were branded 'subhuman' (Untermenschen) parasites who threatened the biological purity of German blood (Blut und Boden) and had to be purged.</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"para-ref\">[1.2]</span> Persecution extended to any group deemed incapable of contributing to the national community (Volksgemeinschaft). Over 10,000 homosexual men were sent to concentration camps, forced to wear pink triangles. Jehovah's Witnesses were imprisoned for refusing military service and Hitler oaths. Under the July 1933 Sterilisation Law, 400,000 disabled or mentally ill citizens were forcibly sterilised, culminating by 1939 in the secret T4 Euthanasia Program, which used gas chambers to murder 70,000 patients.</p>",
